<Base title="Training & Workshops in B2B Sales and AI | Powersales" description="Practical training and workshops for sales teams and management groups in B2B sales, communication and AI support. No theory for theory's sake." lang="en">
  <h1>Training & Workshops</h1>
  <p class="lead">Practical skills for sales teams and management groups. No theory for theory's sake.</p>
  <div class="section">
    <p>Sales training that doesn't lead to changed behaviour is a cost, not an investment. Everything I do is built to be directly applicable — in the next customer meeting, the next pipeline review, the next deal conversation.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="section">
    <h2>Training programmes</h2>
    <h3>B2B Sales and Sales Process</h3>
    <p>How to create, drive and close deals in complex B2B sales. Focus on progression, prioritisation and customer communication that actually works.</p>
    <h3>Communication and Trust in Sales</h3>
    <p>How to communicate in a way that makes customers understand, feel confident and move forward. For salespeople, sales managers and commercial teams.</p>
    <h3>AI in the B2B Sales Process</h3>
    <p>Practical training in how AI support works in reality — without hype, without technical complexity. What to use AI for, how and why.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="section">
    <h2>Workshops</h2>
    <h3>Pipeline Workshop</h3>
    <p>A structured review of your actual pipeline. You leave with concrete next steps per deal and a clearer picture of what's actually going to close.</p>
    <h3>Commercial Clarity</h3>
    <p>For management groups and commercial teams. Who should you win, why should the customer choose you, and what are the most important improvement areas today?</p>
    <h3>AI-Sales OS Onboarding</h3>
    <p>Introduction to Powersales AI-Sales OS for teams that want to get started with AI-supported sales in a structured way.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="section">
    <a href="https://calendly.com/urbgav/30min" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discuss training</a>
  </div>
</Base>
